  "scope": "Actual native Rust service / configured PostgreSQL and owned S3-compatible fixture through counting proxy, one host, random8MiB object; endpoints and tokens excluded.",
  "limitations": [
    "Debug build; timings under shared host load, no production throughput/SLA inference. Small cold samples give empirical order statistics only.",
    "rchar counts all process read syscalls; read_bytes/write_bytes kernel storage accounting can be zero due pagecache; no direct disk device busy measurement.",
    "PostgreSQL active_sql/connection samples match service-owned TCP client ports. pool_status contains the private metrics listener pre-scrape Deadpool counters when available; older binaries return an empty values map. These are approximate concurrent snapshots, not a coherent live-socket or exact queue probe. The sampler itself issues a bounded database metrics snapshot, adding a small observer workload.",
    "CPU ticks are service process CPU including internal worker threads; excludes PostgreSQL/Garage CPU."
